WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.290
Journey twelve: keep listings honest.

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:06.286
Owners publish and are live straight away.

00:00:06.286 --> 00:00:11.067
The Jubilee team looks through what was published, and takes down a

00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:13.778
listing that misrepresents a business.

00:00:14.644 --> 00:00:19.907
Listings shows every published listing, newest first, with its status.

00:00:19.907 --> 00:00:24.794
A name or tagline with a web address or a discount code is tagged

00:00:24.794 --> 00:00:25.396
Flagged.

00:00:26.104 --> 00:00:29.728
A search by name keeps the listings that match.

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:35.445
One listing shows where it stands, its owner and their other listings,

00:00:35.445 --> 00:00:40.221
the flag, and how members see it. Opening it is now written to the audit

00:00:40.221 --> 00:00:42.609
log, with the listing as the reason.

00:00:43.317 --> 00:00:47.585
Take down listing asks for a reason for the owner.

00:00:47.585 --> 00:00:50.061
Without one, nothing is sent.

00:00:50.765 --> 00:00:56.214
With a reason, the listing leaves Jubilee at once, the owner is e-mailed

00:00:56.214 --> 00:01:00.149
why, and the page says so. The owner may list again.

00:01:01.059 --> 00:01:06.094
Behind the screen, each role change made with the jubilee staff command

00:01:06.094 --> 00:01:10.704
is now audited, with its operator and the roles before and after.

00:01:10.704 --> 00:01:12.051
The tests prove it.

00:01:12.911 --> 00:01:18.500
Journey twelve is complete. Nothing in the admin application approves,

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:20.975
declines or verifies a listing.
